.TH SIZE 1
.SH NAME
size \- size of an object file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "size [ object ... ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B size
prints the (decimal) number of bytes required by the text, initialized data, and bss (uninitialized data) portions, and their sum in octal and decimal, of each object-file argument.
If no file is specified,
.B a.out
is used.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
a.out(4), nm(1), strip(1)
.sp
